#
# RK3576 chip options
#

config RK3576_SAI
	bool "SAI (I2S) capture support"
	default n
	---help---
		Enable the SAI2 capture driver used to record from an I2S MEMS
		microphone wired to the 40-pin header (SCLK/LRCK/SDI on pins
		18/26/28).  The AMP slave owns SAI2 exclusively; SAI1 stays with
		Linux for the on-board ES8388 codec.

config RK3576_PDM
	bool "PDM digital microphone capture support"
	default n
	---help---
		Enable the PDM1 capture driver used to record from a PDM MEMS
		microphone wired to the 40-pin header: CLK on GPIO4_A6 (pin 7)
		and GPIO4_B0 (pin 8), DATA on GPIO4_B2 (pin 12).  Those pads
		belong to uart6 and spi4 in the stock device tree, so the AMP
		dtsi disables both.  They are also a 1.8 V IO domain, so the
		microphone must run at 1.8 V or behind a level shifter.

		This is the RK3576's "v2" PDM IP (see rk3576_pdm.c), which
		shares no register layout with the classic Rockchip PDM.

		Takes precedence over RK3576_SAI when both are enabled: the
		microphone demo uses one front end at a time.
